    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "AIGC asset generation (text/image to image/video) and async task result query.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  text2image                  Submit a provider text-to-image asset task. Default is async; use\r\n                              --wait/--poll to wait.\r\n  image2image                 Submit a provider image-to-image asset task with one or more\r\n                              reference images.\r\n  text2video                  Submit a provider text-to-video asset task. Default is async; use\r\n                              --wait/--poll to wait.\r\n  image2video                 Submit an image-to-video task using explicit first/end frames or\r\n                              repeatable reference images.\r\n  query                       Query one AIGC async task by submit id and optionally download\r\n                              artifacts.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc text2image --prompt \"a cat portrait\" --ratio 1:1\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc image2image --image ./input.png --prompt \"turn into watercolor\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc text2video --prompt \"a cat running\" --duration 5s\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc image2video --first-image ./first.png --prompt \"camera push in\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc query --submit-id <submit_id> --download-dir /tmp/out\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Use `lyra-cli media aigc <subcommand> --help` for more information.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "AIGC asset generation (text/image to image/video) and async task result query.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  text2image                  Submit a provider text-to-image asset task. Default is async; use\r\n                              --wait/--poll to wait.\r\n  image2image                 Submit a provider image-to-image asset task with one or more\r\n                              reference images.\r\n  text2video                  Submit a provider text-to-video asset task. Default is async; use\r\n                              --wait/--poll to wait.\r\n  image2video                 Submit an image-to-video task using explicit first/end frames or\r\n                              repeatable reference images.\r\n  query                       Query one AIGC async task by submit id and optionally download\r\n                              artifacts.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc text2image --prompt \"a cat portrait\" --ratio 1:1\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc image2image --image ./input.png --prompt \"turn into watercolor\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc text2video --prompt \"a cat running\" --duration 5s\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc image2video --first-image ./first.png --prompt \"camera push in\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc query --submit-id <submit_id> --download-dir /tmp/out\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Use `lyra-cli media aigc <subcommand> --help` for more information.\r\n",
